      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2005-p2.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Solving \\(2x + 7 = 3\\) gives \\(x = -2.\\)\n\nSubstituting into the second equation, \\(-2b - 10 = -2,\\) so \\(-2b = 8\\) and \\(b = -4.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is B.",
